    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters 2026-06-17 with a lineup anchored by elite speed and favorable LHP matchups. **Corbin Carroll** (79.27) and **Jose Caballero** (74.02) are our highest-projected starters today, both benefiting significantly from their dynamic platoon splits against LHP. While **Corbin Carroll** retains high value despite a moderate LHP penalty, **Jose Caballero** receives a massive +13% boost for his platoon advantage, making him a primary engine for our scarcity-driven SB strategy. **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) and **James Wood** (72.03) round out our top-tier plays; **Seiya Suzuki** thrives against Sullivan\u2019s 4.99 xERA, though we are monitoring a 43% rain risk that could threaten his output, while **James Wood** brings elite 0.407 xwOBA metrics to a favorable matchup against Avila.\n\nOur roster construction leans heavily into these high-efficiency pivots, pushing marginal players like **Dalton Rushing** (41.26) and **Henry Bolte** (41.56) toward the bottom of the order. The most difficult personnel decision centered on **Cole Young**, who fell just short of the cut at 40.07. While **Cole Young** possesses the contact profile we desire, the combination of a tough outing against Kyle Bradish and superior efficiency from **Kyle Karros**\u2014who enjoys park factors and SP skill advantages\u2014effectively relegated **Cole Young** to the pine to protect our innings caps. We remain wary of the weather-impacted games involving **Seiya Suzuki** and **Kyle Karros**, as the 43% rain risk could compress their actual plate appearances. Otherwise, we are well-positioned for an aggressive day on the basepaths, relying on the speed of **Brice Turang** and **Jose Caballero** to manufacture runs despite the defensive presence of elite catchers.",
